    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nI'm having an interesting problem between mini.completion and some of gopls's postfix snippets.\n\nFor example, gopls has a \".split\" postfix snippet that applies to strings, and tries to replace\n```go\nname.split\n```\nwith\n```go\nstrings.Split(name, \"\")\n```\nThere are two parts to the problem. First, the expansion inserts a number of extraneous x characters to the left of the expansion.\n\nIf I complete `name.s<C-Y>`, I get\n```go\nxstrings.Split(name, \"\")\n```\nIf I complete `name.sp<C-Y>`, I get\n```go\nxxstrings.Split(name, \"\")\n```\nAnd so on to `name.split<C-Y>` resulting in\n```go\nxxxxxstrings.Split(name, \"\")\n```\n\nThe number of extraneous leading x characters seems to match the number of characters I've typed for the snippet before invoking expansion.\n\nThe second part of the problem: If the snippet would add N lines somewhere above the edit, some characters get deleted in the line N lines above the edit.\n\nFor example, expanding this snippet adds one new import to the import block:\n\n<img width=\"298\" height=\"256\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/447f09b5-8d1a-4ed5-815f-abd6c9631d9f\" />\n\nIn addition to the inserting extraneous x characters, it also deletes 5 characters from the line above:\n\n<img width=\"314\" height=\"278\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e10ed34b-23e6-4b05-b3a1-42a82b20a49d\" />\n\nThe deleted characters match the positions of the characters I've typed for the snippet.\n\nHere's another example where the snippet adds two new lines, one for the import, and one extra line for formatting. Here's the situation before expanding (I've typed 3 characters of the snippet name):\n\n<img width=\"292\" height=\"218\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3307fbea-6fe7-4e61-a773-bd611e795ef7\" />\n\nAnd the expansion:\n\n<img width=\"340\" height=\"273\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7da08039-e560-4968-950e-cbecf8998142\" />\n\nIn addition to adding 3 extraneous x characters, the edit has also delete 3 characters from the line 2 above the edit:\n\nSo it seems as if the lines are deleted from the line where the cursor was before the expansion added two new lines.\n\nI considered whether the problem might be in gopls (perhaps indicating the wrong range), or in mini.snippets. My guess is that problem is in mini.completion. Here's why I think that:\n- I get the problem with mini.completion, whether it's configured to expand snippets with mini.snippets or vim.snippets.\n- Built-in completion expands this and other postfix snippets correctly with either mini.snippets or vim.snippets.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nI apologize for not providing a minimal config here. It's dinner time and I'm hungry. Let me know if you need a minimal config or any other information from me, and I'll try to provide it within a day or two.",
