            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Seems introduced in <https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/commit/ca7335433ceb16d7eef523338276f23d6aad17f5>. I can reproduce it with that commit on Nvim v0.11.3, but not before it. Here is the minimal configuration:\n\n```lua\n-- Install mini.nvim ...\n\nrequire('mini.completion').setup()\nvim.o.signcolumn = 'yes'\n\n-- https://pkg.go.dev/golang.org/x/tools/gopls\nvim.lsp.config('gopls', {\n  cmd = { 'gopls' },\n  filetypes = { 'go' },\n})\nvim.lsp.enable('gopls')\n```\n\nand steps:\n\n```go\nfunc main() {\n\ttest := \"string string\"\n\t// 1) type: test.spli\n\t//               ^^ corresponds to how many 'x' will be prepended\n\t// 2) select: split!\n\t// 3) confirm with any character\n\ttest.spl\n}\n```\n\nYou can also find them [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/compare/ca7335433ceb16d7eef523338276f23d6aad17f5...loichyan:mini.nvim:issue/1948).",
