            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> * Are you sure you don't have another autocompletion plugin/functionality enabled? _Just_ after typing `func`, the completion menu adds three more entries (plus one _just_ before the snippet session is started). However, info window is not adjusted, which makes me think that this doesn't come from 'mini.completion'.\n\nI don't think I have other autocompletion enabled. But I enabled on_type_formatting recently, not sure if that has any impact or not.\n\n> * What other LSP server do you have attached here? My guess would be the one from 'mini.snippets' (the `func` snippet is the same as in 'friendly-snippets').\n\nBy LSP server, I think it should be `gopls`. Below is part of the output from `LspInfo`.\n```bash\nvim.lsp: Active Clients ~\n- mini.snippets (id: 1)\n  - Version: ? (no serverInfo.version response)\n  - Root directory: ~/workspace/forgejo/swahpy/dl-go\n  - Command: <function @/home/wanghy/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:2646>\n  - Settings: {}\n  - Attached buffers: 10, 13\n- gopls (id: 2)\n```\nFor the snippets, yes I use friendly-snippets.\n\n> * Can you please clarify which 'completeopt' you have set and which keys you press to accept completion item?\n\no.completeopt = 'menuone,noinsert,fuzzy'\nAnd I use `Tab` for completion. Just because of this, I adjusted the completeopt to the current one.\n\nAnyway, I'm not so confident to ensure all your questions have been answered properly, so here is my neovim [setup](https://github.com/swahpy/mvim/blob/8040125955ed9779fd077997df4b59e26e34b2ef/lua/plugins/mini.lua#L207). If possible you could find something wrong there. Thank you!",
