            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Anyway, I'm not so confident to ensure all your questions have been answered properly, so here is my neovim [setup](https://github.com/swahpy/mvim/blob/8040125955ed9779fd077997df4b59e26e34b2ef/lua/plugins/mini.lua#L207). If possible you could find something wrong there. Thank you!\n\nNope, still can not reproduce when using config as is, I am afraid :( I was able to reproduce the candidate list when typing `f`-`u`-`n`-`c` in the Go file that contains `import ( \"strings\" )`, but still no signs of what I noticed in the previous comment.\n\nAnother question: do you have not-so-performant machine or a large Go project, by any chance?\n\nMy current hypothesis is that this *might* be related to using `noinsert` instead of `noselect` in combination with slow results. Maybe it doesn't trigger some condition/callback/event.",
