        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Another question: do you have not-so-performant machine or a large Go project, by any chance?\n\nThe machine is sufficient and the project is not a big one actually.\n\n> My current hypothesis is that this _might_ be related to using `noinsert` instead of `noselect` in combination with slow results. Maybe it doesn't trigger some condition/callback/event.\n\nOk, let me revert the configuration to try. I set `completeopt` to this is I want to use `TAB` to complete the suggestion. If `noinsert` is not set, then the input is a total mess without `noselect`. Because by default it will select one and the selected will trigger more candidates and then insert.",
