        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I set `completeopt` to this is I want to use `TAB` to complete the suggestion. If `noinsert` is not set, then the input is a total mess without `noselect`. Because by default it will select one and the selected will trigger more candidates and then insert.\n\nThis is possible (and [suggested](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/68955a915c45ae7c988c539abe6e89f0971a9a2d/doc/mini-completion.txt#L87-L89)) with `noselect` flag. Something like this:\n\n```lua\nvim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,noselect,fuzzy,nosort'\nlocal map_multistep = require('mini.keymap').map_multistep\nmap_multistep('i', '<Tab>', { 'pmenu_next' })\nmap_multistep('i', '<S-Tab>', { 'pmenu_prev' })\n```\n\nWith 'mini.completion' there is (usually) no need to explicitly confirm/accept the candidate: non-snippets are already inserted, snippets are inserted after any non-keyword key. One possible difference is that this approach doesn't immediately show info window, which has pros and cons:\n- Saves extra not needed requests to LSP server.\n- Additional text edits (like auto-import) require [info window to be shown](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/68955a915c45ae7c988c539abe6e89f0971a9a2d/doc/mini-completion.txt#L449-L455), so adjust delay accordingly.",
